# Local-only secrets for `wrangler dev`. Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in.
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored and must stay that way. It is read by the Worker at
# runtime, never bundled, and never reaches the browser — the Sky panel talks
# only to /api/sky on our own origin and receives an answer plus source links.
#
# PRODUCTION DOES NOT USE THIS FILE. Set the real key as a Cloudflare secret,
# which is encrypted at rest and not visible in the dashboard afterwards:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put SKY_API_KEY
#
# Rotate it by running that again; no deploy is needed. If it ever leaks,
# revoke at the provider first and rotate second — revoking is what stops the
# spend, rotating only stops the old key being useful.

# The provider key Sky uses. Absent or empty = Sky reports itself unavailable
# rather than answering, which is the correct failure: it never invents an
# answer from retrieved passages without a model.
SKY_API_KEY=

# Optional. Which model to call. Kept server-side with the key so the browser
# never learns it.
SKY_MODEL=
